DESCRIPTION:What does it sound like under the ocean? 🌊\n\n \n\nOn Saturd
 ay\, July 25\, join artist Madeleine Popkin in a special Saturday Sparks e
 xploration of underwater sounds recorded off the coast of Beaufort\, North
  Carolina! Madeleine will pair her paintings with visitor listening statio
 ns featuring recordings by marine bioacoustics researcher Dr. Shannon Brow
 n. An ambient soundscape\, composed of underwater recordings from North Ca
 rolina’s coast\, will immerse you in a watery world.\n\nYou can meet Mad
 eleine in the Morehead Planetarium Gateway Gallery from 1 to 4 p.m. as she
  presents her project and the power of combining art and science.\n\n \n\n
 🎟️ All ages are welcome. This special program is included with admiss
 ion.\n\n🎨 This project is supported by the North Carolina Arts Council\
 , a division of the NC Department of Natural & Cultural Resources.\n\n \n\
 nABOUT SATURDAY SCIENCE SPARKS\n\nMORE is happening at Morehead this year!
  New for 2026\, Saturday Science Sparks offers Morehead guests a closer en
 counter with current science. Covering topics like astronomy\, the physics
  of juggling\, and computer science\, this program collaborates with commu
 nitxy partners and academic clubs\, bringing you up-close experiences in t
 he exciting world of STEAM. Saturday Science Sparks is open to the public 
 and included in admission.
GEO:35.913753;-79.050409
LOCATION:Morehead Planetarium and Science Center
SUMMARY:Saturday Science Sparks — Coastal Frequencies
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/saturday-science-sparks-coasta
 l-frequencies
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
