DTEND:20260729T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:People have a powerful need to understand and predict their env
 ironments in order to feel in control. When we are exposed to potential th
 reats to our well-being\, we naturally respond to this uncertainty with an
 xiety and fear. This training will address ways of effectively coping with
  uncertainty in today’s media-saturated world. The course will examine h
 ow to remain positive and functional despite the risks of living in a chan
 ging world. Included will be practical tips for coping with uncertainty\, 
 re-establishing control and how to speak to children about fear.\n\n \n\nC
 lick on Carolina Talent registration link and select the “Request” but
 ton to automatically enroll.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Coping During Uncertain Times
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/coping-during-uncertain-times-
 9017
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52940891056803
DTSTART:20260729T160000Z
DTEND:20260729T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Launch your systematic review with free summer series! \n\n \n\
 nInterested in conducting a systematic review? The Health Sciences Library
 ’s Systematic Review Summer Workshop Series will get you started in eigh
 t bite-sized sessions. Sign up for all of them\, or just the ones you need
 . \n\n \n\nThis free virtual series will provide researchers with tools an
 d resources to confidently navigate the systematic review process.  \n\n \
 n\nWho should attend? \n\n \n\nThis series is intended for individuals and
  research teams who are planning to conduct a systematic literature review
  or want more information about systematic reviews. It is also relevant fo
 r those conducting scoping reviews or other similar evidence synthesis pro
 jects. No prior knowledge or experience with systematic reviews is require
 d. The instruction is aimed toward health reviews\, but open to anyone at 
 UNC-Chapel Hill or the UNC Medical Center.   \n\n \n\nWhat will be covered
 ? \n\n \n\nWe’ve broken down the systematic review process from ideation
  through publication into eight one-hour lessons. Each lunchtime session r
 uns on Wednesdays from noon to 1 p.m. \n\n \n\nJune 10 - Introduction to S
 ystematic Review Methods \n\nJune 17 - What Type of Review Should You Choo
 se? \n\nJune 24 - Project Management and Helpful Tools for Conducting Syst
 ematic Reviews \n\nJuly 8 - Literature Searching for Systematic Reviews \n
 \nJuly 15 - Introduction to Covidence \n\nJuly 22 - Managing Data\, Writin
 g and Publishing your Review \n\nJuly 29 - Predictive Artificial Intellige
 nce and Automation Tools
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Predictive Artificial Intelligence and Automation Tools (Class 7 of
  8 in the Systematic Review Summer Workshop Series)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/predictive-artificial-intellig
 ence-and-automation-tools-class-7-of-8-in-the-systematic-review-summer-wor
 kshop-series
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
