DTEND:20260812T150000Z
DESCRIPTION:This webinar introduces the fundamentals of social network anal
 ysis within the context of community-engaged evaluation research. It will 
 begin with the underlying theory behind networks and how we build them wit
 h an emphasis on relationships\, trust\, and community connections. We'll 
 share several case studies to illustrate how we use networks in impact rep
 orting and evaluation research. Participants will gain insight into how ne
 twork approaches can center community voices\, connect partnerships\, and 
 enhance evaluation practices.\n\n \n\nRegister for Circles of Influence!\n
 \n \n\nBernard Coles is presenting. \n\n \n\nThis session is part of the C
 onnections that Count: Abacus Evaluation Community Engagement Webinar Seri
 es.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Circles of Influence: Social Network Analysis for Community-Engaged
  Evaluation Research
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/circles-of-influence-social-ne
 twork-analysis-for-community-engaged-evaluation-research
