DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52638987481885
DTSTART:20260909T130000Z
DTEND:20260909T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course will take place over two days (9/9/2026 and 9/11/20
 26) and will be offered via Zoom. Attendance is required as the course wil
 l not be recorded.\n\nNesting can arise from hierarchical data structures 
 (e.g.\, siblings nested within family\; patients nested within therapist)\
 , longitudinal data structures (repeated measures nested within individual
 )\, or both (repeated measures nested within patient and patient nested wi
 thin therapist).\n\nIt is well known that the analysis of nested data stru
 ctures using traditional general linear models (e.g.\, ANOVA or regression
 ) is flawed\, oftentimes substantially so: Tests of significance are likel
 y biased and within- and between-group effects are confounded with one ano
 ther. All of these limitations can be addressed within the multilevel mode
 l.\n\nIn this workshop\, we provide an introduction to the application of 
 multilevel models with nested data\, including software implementation in 
 SAS\, SPSS and Stata.\n\nRegistration and fee required for Zoom link acces
 s.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Multilevel Modeling 
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-multilevel-mod
 eling-6356
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53443710857131
DTSTART:20260909T140000Z
DTEND:20260909T160000Z
DESCRIPTION:This online training session will provide an introduction to qu
 alitative research methods. Participants will have the opportunity to ask 
 questions and share experiences conducting qualitative research. Topics in
 clude: differences between quantitative and qualitative research\, qualita
 tive research methodologies\, strategies for qualitative data collection\,
  & methods of qualitative data analysis.\n\n \n\nThis event is part of the
  NC TraCS Qualitative Research Training Series and may be recorded. Materi
 als such as slides or handouts will be shared with documented attendees on
 ly.\n\n \n\nPresenters:\nMaryBeth Grewe\, MPH\nProgram Manager\, Qualitati
 ve Research Service\nResearch Specialist\, Patient and Community Engagemen
 t in Research (PaCER) Program\n\n \n\nSimone Frank\, MPH\nSenior Project M
 anager\, Patient and Community Engagement in Research (PaCER) Program\nRes
 earch Specialist\, Qualitative Research Service\n\n \n\nRegister\n\n \n\nP
 lease contact MaryBeth Grewe at marybeth_grewe@med.unc.edu if you have que
 stions about this training.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Qualitative Research 101
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/qualitative-research-101-5084
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53107617656740
DTSTART:20260909T160000Z
DTEND:20260909T170000Z
DESCRIPTION:Stressful situations\, whether from internal or external source
 s\, are inevitable in organizations. For some managers\, this may lead to 
 over-extending themselves with minimal time for self-care.\nThis training 
 offers tools to help managers cope with stress and thrive in their organiz
 ations.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Self-Care Tips for Managers
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/self-care-tips-for-managers-64
 17
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
