DTSTART:20260915T140000Z
DTEND:20260915T153000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course is only open to the UNC Chapel Hill Community. You 
 must have an active ONYEN to register. \n\n \n\nAI in Research: Driving In
 novation Forward\n\nDiscover how artificial intelligence can streamline wo
 rkflows\, uncover hidden patterns\, and empower breakthroughs in your fiel
 d. Learn practical applications of AI through Odum Institute AIR series th
 at can revolutionize your research process.\n\nThis course will introduce 
 participants to generative AI tools in qualitative software—ATLAS.ti\, M
 AXQDA\, and NVivo. These tools can be used to summarize textual documents 
 through AI-assisted memo writing and to support coding\, with each program
  taking a different approach to integrating human judgment and AI features
 .\n\nThe course will also demonstrate how ChatGPT can be used to code text
 ual data\, how to create effective prompts\, and how to import results fro
 m ChatGPT into qualitative software for further analysis. The course will 
 be based on presentation and lecture but will provide brief exercises for 
 hands-on exercises to be completed outside of the course.\n\nRegistration 
 is required to secure your spot and receive Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:AI in Research series – Introduction to AI Tools in Qualitative S
 oftware
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ai-in-research-series-introduc
 tion-to-ai-tools-in-qualitative-software-4936
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
