UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_52692517581271
DTSTART:20261005T140000Z
DTEND:20261005T163000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course will cover two days (10/5/26 and 10/7/26). Attendan
 ce is required as the course will not be recorded.\n\nThis course introduc
 es students to Stata and data management. It is tailored for non-users who
  want to learn how to manage data more effectively. Each day\, the class w
 ill demonstrate how to use the commands\, followed by hands-on exercises u
 sing sample datasets. By the end of the course\, participants will be able
  to perform the following:• Use Stata’s Graphical User Interference (G
 UI) with dialog boxes\n• Run Stata commands from the command window and 
 from scripts (“do” files)\n• Enter\, transfer\, and save data in dif
 ferent formats\, e.g.\, Excel\, SAS\, SPSS\, text files\n• Inspect the c
 ontents of a Stata dataset\n• Append\, merge\, and sort datasets\n• Id
 entify and clean duplicate records\n• Calculate new variables\n• Creat
 e and manage labels for variables and values\n• Recode variables\n• Wo
 rk with blocks of observations (“by” processing)\n• Perform row-wise
  calculations (groups of columns)\n• Collapse data into summary tables\n
 • Reshape between long and wide formats\n• Save and reproduce your wor
 k with “do” files\n• Obtain descriptive statistics\n• Create graph
 s and tables\n• Run basic statistical analyses\, e.g.\, Ordinary Least S
 quares regression\, correlation matrices\, Chi-square tests\, t-tests\n\nR
 egistration and fee (refundable for students) are required for Zoom link a
 ccess.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Stata
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-stata
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53379073694562
DTSTART:20261005T233000Z
DTEND:20261006T010000Z
DESCRIPTION:Jada Pinkett Smith\, Queen Latifah\, and Vivica A. Fox anchor t
 his energetic reworking of the heist film. After a series of setbacks leav
 es four Black women with few viable paths forward\, they embark on a strin
 g of increasingly audacious bank robberies. Blending humor\, suspense\, an
 d tragedy\, Set It Off captures both the bonds of friendship and the press
 ures of race\, gender\, and economic inequality in 1990s urban America. \n
 This film will be introduced by Professor Daelena Tinnin-Gadson\, UNC-Chap
 el Hill Department of English and Comparative Literature. \nIt will be scr
 eened at 7:30 p.m. at The Lumina Theater (620 Market St\, Chapel Hill\, NC
  27516). Tickets are free for all audience members\, and registration is r
 equired via The Lumina’s webpage. When this link is live\, click to rese
 rve your free ticket. \nUNC-Chapel Hill students can receive CLE credit fo
 r attending by scanning the QR code at the event. \n  \nAbout the Series: 
 \nJoin the Ackland Film Forum this fall for Crime Thrillers from the Ameri
 cas: Snapshots of Social Anxiety\, a series that accompanies the Ackland e
 xhibition Care and Concern: Recent Acquisitions of Modern and Contemporary
  Art. \nAs vehicles of social commentary and stylistic bravura\, crime thr
 illers often register the pressures and contradictions of their historical
  moment. Across nearly half a century\, the films in this series stage enc
 ounters with political power\, public trust\, inequality\, and ambition th
 rough assassination plots\, botched robberies\, and media-driven spectacle
 . \nFrom the crises of the late 1960s to the intensified media environment
 s of the twenty-first century\, these works show how genre cinema can capt
 ure social anxiety in real time. Each film stands both as a gripping narra
 tive and as a record of a world under strain\, where institutions falter a
 nd everyday life becomes fraught with conflict. \nThe Ackland Film Forum i
 s co-organized by the Ackland Art Museum and UNC Film Studies\, housed in 
 the UNC-Chapel Hill Department of English and Comparative Literature.
LOCATION:The Lumina Theater\, 620 Market Street\, Chapel Hill\, 27516\, Uni
 ted States
SUMMARY:Ackland Film Forum: "Set It Off" (F. Gary Gray\, 1996)
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/ackland-film-forum-set-it-off-
 f-gary-gray-1996
CATEGORIES:Exhibits
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
X-SOURCE:UNC Chapel Hill
DTSTAMP:20260731T040457Z
UID:tag:localist.com\,2008:EventInstance_53055342985349
