DTSTART:20261013T130000Z
DTEND:20261013T190000Z
DESCRIPTION:This course introduces participants to constructivist grounded 
 theory (CGT). Grounded theory (GT) methods consist of flexible guidelines 
 to fit particular research problems\, not to apply mechanically. With thes
 e guidelines\, you expedite and systematize data collection and analysis. 
 GT methods can assist researchers in making their work more analytic\, pre
 cise\, and compelling.\n\nIn this course\, following an exploration of the
  history and development of GT\, we examine GT basic guidelines and major 
 strategies\, including initial line-by-line and focused coding\, the use o
 f gerunds\, memoing\, diagramming\, theoretical sampling\, and categorizin
 g. Throughout the sessions\, there is an emphasis on CGT’s epistemologic
 al foundation and resultant adaptations to the research process\, includin
 g regarding the literature review\, researcher positionality/ies and refle
 xivity\, and participant involvement.\n\nThe course will include a number 
 of hands-on exercises to exemplify\, and give participants an opportunity 
 to practice\, the strategies being discussed. For the coding exercise\, yo
 u may bring and use some of your own qualitative data\, or if you do not h
 ave data yet\, some will be supplied. Clear guidelines and support are pro
 vided to course participants with regard to all aspects of CGT.\n\nThe ses
 sions will utilize CGT readings and resources from Kathy Charmaz\, Robert 
 Thornberg\, Adele Clarke\, and myself\, and will draw on the extensive sch
 olarship of Barney Glaser and Anselm Strauss. A pack of materials will be 
 shared with participants in advance of the course. This course will be of 
 interest to those doing full CGT studies but also to those who may be inte
 rested in learning about and potentially using some of the powerful GT str
 ategies (such as coding) in studies with a different overall methodologica
 l approach.\n\nRegistration and fee (refundable for UNCCH students) are re
 quired for Zoom link access.
LOCATION:
SUMMARY:Introduction to Constructivist Grounded Theory
URL;VALUE=URI:https://calendar.unc.edu/event/introduction-to-constructivist
 -grounded-theory-5530
CATEGORIES:Workshops and Classes
END:VEVENT
